From cda702273e77f8fe1c2792b19bd414b0f02f237a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:02:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fuse multi-CTA disk Engram step and wire packed/cached rows

Upstream base: a75357bba81e31e4f3085700f94b6a0b29aed44a

Rationale:
1. Fuse disk Engram wait, FP8 gather/dequantize, and release into a single multi-CTA TileLang kernel (engram_rows_step_kernel) with exact column-divisor block sizing (384 threads for TP4, 512 threads for TP3/TP1), overlapped device-memory row-ID preload, and 128B-isolated GPU-L2 inter-CTA synchronization so only CTA 0 polls mapped-host control on wait and only the last finishing CTA writes mapped-host control on release.
2. Wire ParallelEngramEmbedding.open_disk_rows() to register rank-compacted 4 KiB-page-aligned (15 x 264B rows/page) single-plane packed sources via add_packed_source() when SPARK_DS41F_ENGRAM_PACKED_DIR is configured or a pre-packed file is present alongside the checkpoint, preserving standard two-plane O_DIRECT loading by default.
3. Remove the 64-token (1536-lookup) PLE_CACHE_MAX_LOOKUPS bypass in _row_plan.h by sizing miss scratch arrays to max(max_lookups, PLE_CACHE_MAX_LOOKUPS), keeping the 17.3 MiB 4-way set-associative user-space row cache active across all batch sizes.

Quality implications: Bit-exact (torch.equal) with the 3-launch disk Engram path and two-plane reader.

Tests: pytest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_engram_rows.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py and compute-sanitizer memcheck/initcheck/racecheck.

Upstream status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 disk Engram optimization.
